description:
FILED s521a (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-18) from the #3433 probes.  PRE-EXISTING (same on a5885afc).

  my $r1 = \*FOO; my $r2 = \*FOO; bless $r1, "Y"; print ref($r2), " ", ref(\*FOO), "\n";
  open FH, "<", "/dev/null"; my $h = \*FH; bless $h, "Q"; print ref(\*FH), "\n";
perl: `Y Y` / `Q`.  PCL: `GLOB GLOB` / `GLOB`.

CAUSE: `*FOO` emits `(p-make-typeglob "main" "FOO")`, which builds a NEW p-typeglob struct each time; #3433 records a glob's bless class on the struct (EQ, *p-handle-stash*), which is right for gensym and `\do { local *FH }` (each a distinct glob in perl too) but cannot see a second mention of the same NAMED glob.  The fix is glob IDENTITY (one struct per stash entry, or a key that is the stash entry's symbol for a named, non-localized glob) -- the #423 glob-representation family; do NOT key by name alone: `\do { local *FH }` twice must stay two objects (probed: perl GLOB|X).
